QuestGuidance.Register("en",365,{
[11649]="70064509\n1\tDestroy vile phial of bile (total: 12)\030Defeat Thaurisgar creatures (total: 12)\tTorvendor has asked you to cleanse Thaurisgar of vile remnants. Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary is in Carn Dûm.\n2\tReturn to Torvendor\tYou have put down as many foul creatures as you could within the Thaurisgar. Torvendor should be informed immediately. Torvendor is located at Bail Avarc, outside of Carn Dûm.\n",
[11650]="70064507\n1\tCollect research notes (total: 6)\tBaranoth has asked you to collect any research notes that remain in tact within Thaurisgar. Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary is in Carn Dûm.\n2\tReturn to Baranoth\tThese research notes should be enough for Baranoth to examine. Baranoth is located at Bail Avarc, outside of Carn Dûm.\n",
[11651]="7002C7D2\n1\tPenda is at the Rohirrim-camp along the road near the north base of the Cuthstan ridge. Penda believes that there may be clues around the Rohirrim-camp that could reveal what may have happened to cause his companions to leave so suddenly.\t\n2\tReturn to Penda to discuss your findings\tYou have collected sufficient evidence and should now return to Penda.\n3\tReturn to Penda to discuss your findings\tPenda is at the Rohirrim-camp along the road near the north base of the Cuthstan ridge. You have discovered a few clues around the abandoned camp and should report your findings to Penda.\n4\tPenda has asked you to search for clues to the west of the Rohirrim-camp.\t\n5\tReturn to Penda with the results of your search\tYou have collected sufficient evidence and should now return to Penda.\n6\tReturn to Penda with the results of your search\tPenda is at the Rohirrim-camp along the road near the north base of the Cuthstan ridge. You have discovered a few clues while investigating outside of the Rohirrim-camp. You should return to Penda and report your findings to him.\n",
[11652]="7002AED0\n1\tBring some special Yule cheer to the snow-beasts (0/3)\tThe snow-beasts can be found to the east of Winter-home. Guard Kember wants you to bring some special Yule cheer to the snow-beasts of Frostbluff.\n2\tAwakened from a deep sleep by your cheers, the snow-beast has moved to a less noisy area. The beast seems to have no intention of leaving Frostbluff. Perhaps a little more cheer will help.\t\n3\tBring some special Yule cheer to the snow-beasts (1/3)\tThe snow-beast has fallen back asleep. A bit more Yule cheer might drive him off.\n4\tAwakened from a deep sleep yet again, the beast has moved to a less noisy area. The beast still seems to have no intention of leaving Frostbluff. Perhaps a little more cheer will help.\t\n5\tBring some special Yule cheer to the snow-beasts (2/3)\tThe snow-beast has fallen asleep again. A bit more Yule cheer might drive him off.\n6\tThe beast has moved to a less noisy area and is completely unmoved by your repeated attempts to drive him off. You should return to Guard Kember and explain the situation.\t\n7\tTalk to Guard Kember\tThe beasts are no longer responding to your cheers. You should return to Guard Kember and ask him what to do next.\n",
[11653]="7004BD97\n1\tDescend into the Black Pits of Mordor\tThe Order of the Eye has entered the Abyss of Mordath to seek vengeance upon King Váskmun Greytooth and lay claim to the lost artifacts of the Dark Lord. They have pursued the Firehorns into the depths of the Black Pits of Mordor.\n2\tCross the Abyss and pass into Thol Shíkug, the Screaming Deep\tThe Order of the Eye has crossed the Abyss dividing the Black Pits into a towering structure built into the foundations of Barad-dûr.\n3\tDefeat the Order of the Eye in Murpraush, the Hall of Spoiling, and ascend the Black Stairs of Durshnúl\tThe Order of the Eye has laid claim to Thol Shíkug and descended into Murpraush, the Hall of Spoiling. They must be defeated if you are to continue your pursuit of King Greytooth and Firehorns.\n4\tDefeat Sagróg, the Bitter Warden, and enter the Ring-prisons in pursuit of the Firehorns\tAs Sauron willed for King Greytooth and the Firehorns to pass unhindered deeper into the Mordath, Sagróg, the Bitter Warden, stands in your path. You must overcome him to continue your pursuit of King Greytooth and his folk.\n5\tConfront King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns in Glurnákh, The Pit of Greed\tKing Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns have descended into Glurnákh, The Pit of Greed. You must force King Greytooth to see reason or defeat him before he can lay claim to the Dwarf-ring, Manthríf.\n6\tCompleted: Abyss of Mordath (Tier 1)\tYou have completed the Abyss of Mordath on Tier 1 and prevented the Dwarf-rings from being wielded to any evil end.\n",
[11654]="7004BD98\n1\tDescend into the Black Pits of Mordor\tThe Order of the Eye has entered the Abyss of Mordath to seek vengeance upon King Váskmun Greytooth and lay claim to the lost artifacts of the Dark Lord. They have pursued the Firehorns into the depths of the Black Pits of Mordor.\n2\tCross the Abyss and pass into Thol Shíkug, the Screaming Deep\tThe Order of the Eye has crossed the Abyss dividing the Black Pits into a towering structure built into the foundations of Barad-dûr.\n3\tDefeat the Order of the Eye in Murpraush, the Hall of Spoiling, and ascend the Black Stairs of Durshnúl\tThe Order of the Eye has laid claim to Thol Shíkug and descended into Murpraush, the Hall of Spoiling. They must be defeated if you are to continue your pursuit of King Greytooth and Firehorns.\n4\tDefeat Sagróg, the Bitter Warden, and enter the Ring-prisons in pursuit of the Firehorns\tAs Sauron willed for King Greytooth and the Firehorns to pass unhindered deeper into the Mordath, Sagróg, the Bitter Warden, stands in your path. You must overcome him to continue your pursuit of King Greytooth and his folk.\n5\tConfront King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns in Glurnákh, The Pit of Greed\tKing Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns have descended into Glurnákh, The Pit of Greed. You must force King Greytooth to see reason or defeat him before he can lay claim to the Dwarf-ring, Manthríf.\n6\tCompleted: Abyss of Mordath (Tier 2)\tYou have completed the Abyss of Mordath on Tier 2 and prevented the Dwarf-rings from being wielded to any evil end.\n",
[11655]="7001B51E\n1\tConfront the condemned villager once more\tThe condemned villager is in the accursed village of Audaghaim, in the Dourstocks, east of the Haunted Inn. You should confront the condemned villager once more, this time armed with full knowledge of the truth he strove to conceal.\n2\tTalk to Prestadír at the Haunted Inn\tPrestadír awaits you at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, west of Audaghaim. You should speak with Prestadír and tell him that the evil past of Audaghaim has been confronted at last.\n",
[11656]="700372D2\n1\tEquip bucket and extinguish fires in the western fields of the Broadacres (total: 12)\tFires can be found throughout the fields west of Stoke in the Broadacres. Reeve Fríthild has asked you to ride out and extinguish the fires that the Warg-riders started in the Broadacres.\n",
[11657]="700687C5\n1\tPick leafy vines from trellises (total: 8)\tHasna has asked you to pick leafy vines from trellises. However, you must avoid being spotted by gardeners more than a few times. The trellises can be found around the eastern side of the Tor-gardens pool. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Hasna at the Dahâl Huliz\tYou have gathered many leafy vines. You should bring them back to Hasna at the Dahâl Huliz.\n3\tTalk to Phêrida Iron-edge\tHasna is too nervous to give Phêrida Iron-edge the vine circlet and has asked you to go instead. Phêrida can be found at the Dahâl Huliz.\n",
[11658]="70059404\n1\tLook for Stomper\tStomper the pony has fled into the western Wildwood. You should look for signs of Stomper's flight.\n2\tFollow Stomper's trail\tHoof-prints may be found in the Wildwood. You should look for more prints from Stomper the pony.\n3\tFollow Stomper's trail\tHoof-prints may be found in the Wildwood. You should look for more prints from Stomper the pony.\n4\tTalk to Minda Heathertoes\tMinda is in the western Wildwood. You should talk to Minda Heathertoes.\n5\tDefeat Wildwood pony-stalkers (total: 4)\tWildwood pony-stalkers can be found in Wildwood. Minda Heathertoes has asked you to defeat the Wargs hunting Stomper the pony.\n6\tTalk to Minda Heathertoes\tMinda can be found in the western Wildwood. You should talk to Minda Heathertoes.\n7\tTalk to Minda Heathertoes\tMinda can be found near a pond in the central Wildwood. You should talk to Minda Heathertoes.\n",
[11659]="7006C5D0\n1\tSpeak with the sage Thridarlan in Shonith\030Speak with the quartermaster Alidal\tDagortas, an elder among the Kintai Elves asked you to introduce yourself to her assistants Thridarlan and Alidal. Each plays an important role in measuring and rewarding the value of those who aid the Kintai in the Valley of Ikorbân.\n2\tReturn to and speak with Dagortas in Shonith\tYou spoke with Thridarlan and Alidal. You should return to the elder Elf, Dagortas. She will be pleased to know you met her assistants in Shonith.\n",
[11660]="700466ED\n1\tTalk to Duinhir\030Talk to Wídfara\030Talk to Gléowine\030Talk to Gamling\030Talk to Cutha\tAsk Duinhir, Gléowine, Wídfara, Gamling, and Cutha about what they saw of the battle yesterday. They can all be found among the tents of Aragorn's Pavilion.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor. You should return to Aragorn and tell him what you learned.\n3\tComplete -- The Aftermath: Dervorin and Rossaran\030Complete -- The Aftermath: Forlong, Golasgil, and Hirluin\030Complete -- The Aftermath: Ingold and Turgon\030Complete -- The Aftermath: Duilin and Derufin\030Complete -- Book 7, Chapter 2: The Council of the Captains\tAragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor. Help Aragorn survey the battlefield for the missing and presumed dead of Gondor.\n4\tTalk to Rossaran\030Talk to Dervorin\030Talk to Golasgil\030Talk to Ingold\tYou should speak with Rossaran, Dervorin, Golasgil, and Ingold, who can all be found in Aragorn's Pavilion, upon the after-battle Pelennor.\n5\tTalk to Aragorn\tYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n6\tComplete -- The Aftermath: Elfmar, Harding, and Torferth\030Complete -- The Aftermath: The Valiant Rohirrim\tAragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor. Help Aragorn survey the battlefield for the missing and presumed dead of Rohan.\n7\tTalk to Éomer\030Talk to Nothmar\tYou should talk to Éomer and Nothmar, who can be found at Aragorn's Pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n8\tTalk to Aragorn\tYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n",
[11661]="700466EA\n1\tFind Dervorin\030Find Rossaran\tSearch for Dervorin and Rossaran on the after-battle Pelennor.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor. You should return to Aragorn now that Dervorin and Rossaran are found.\n",
[11662]="700466EE\n1\tTalk to Duinhir\tYou should speak with Duinhir, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n2\tIdentify Duilin\030Identify Derufin\tSearch among the slain for Duilin and Derufin's bodies.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn can be found in his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor. You should return to Aragorn now that you have identified Duilin and Derufin.\n",
[11663]="700466EF\n1\tFind Elfmar\030Find Harding\030Find Torferth\tElfmar, Harding, Torferth were last seen somewhere on the Pelennor Fields. Look for them there, after the battle.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn\tYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n",
[11664]="700466F0\n1\tFind Golasgil\030Find Hirluin\tSearch for Golasgil and Hirluin on the after-battle Pelennor.\n2\tFind Forlong\tSearch for Forlong on the after-battle Pelennor.\n3\tBlow Forlong's horn\tForlong lies dying on the after-battle Pelennor. Blow Forlong's horn to summon Thorongil.\n4\tTalk to Aragorn\tYou should talk to Aragorn, who stands by Forlong on the after-battle Pelennor.\n",
[11665]="700466E8\n1\tFind Ingold\030Find Turgon\tSearch for Ingold and Turgon on the after-battle Pelennor.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn can be found in his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor. You should return to Aragorn now that you have found Ingold and Turgon.\n",
[11666]="700466EC\n1\tFind Grimbold\030Find Déorwine\030Find Dúnhere\030Find Guthláf\030Find Herefara\030Find Herubrand\030Find Nothmar\tGrimbold, Déorwine, Dúnhere, Guthláf, Herefara, and Herubrand died on the Pelennor. Nothmar is missing. Search for the valiant Rohirrim on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn\tYou should talk to Aragorn, who can be found at his pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n",
[11667]="70022B51\n1\tPlay tricks to scare the hobbits in the Haunted Burrow (total: 6)\tScared hobbits are all over the Haunted Burrow, and surely there is a way to frighten them, because it is funny. You should harry and harass the hobbits.\n2\tTell Ráthgeir of your hilarious escapades\tRáthgeir, a mean sort of dwarf, can be found outside the Haunted Burrow, hiding behind some crates. You should tell Ráthgeir all about the little pranks you pulled.\n",
[11668]="70021A00\n1\tTalk to Bjarni at The Prancing Pony\tBjarni is at The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree. You should speak with Bjarni if you wish to properly join the Ale Association.\n",
[11669]="70021A06\n1\tTalk to Finn in Staddle\tFinn is in Staddle, near the town of Bree. You should speak with Finn to continue the Ale Association Challenge at his tasting location.\n2\tDrink beers (0/6)\tThe beers are in Staddle Centre. Finn has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n3\tDrink beers (1/6)\tThe beers are in Staddle Centre. Finn has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n4\tDrink beers (2/6)\tThe beers are in Staddle Centre. Finn has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n5\tDrink beers (3/6)\tThe beers are in Staddle Centre. Finn has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n6\tDrink beers (4/6)\tThe beers are in Staddle Centre. Finn has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n7\tDrink beers (5/6)\tThe beers are in Staddle Centre. Finn has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n8\tTalk to Finn at Staddle Centre\tFinn is in the centre of Staddle. You should speak with Finn to receive further instructions on the Ale Association Challenge.\n",
[11670]="70021A02\n1\tTalk to Daggeir at the Combe-gate\tDaggeir is at the Combe-gate in Bree. You should speak with Daggeir to continue the Ale Association Challenge.\n2\tDrink beers (0/6)\tThe beers are at the Combe-gate in Bree. Daggeir has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n3\tDrink beers (1/6)\tThe beers are at the Combe-gate in Bree. Daggeir has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n4\tDrink beers (2/6)\tThe beers are at the Combe-gate in Bree. Daggeir has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n5\tDrink beers (3/6)\tThe beers are at the Combe-gate in Bree. Daggeir has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n6\tDrink beers (4/6)\tThe beers are at the Combe-gate in Bree. Daggeir has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n7\tDrink beers (5/6)\tThe beers are at the Combe-gate in Bree. Daggeir has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n8\tTalk to Daggeir at the Combe-gate\tDaggeir is at the Combe-gate in Bree. You should speak with Daggeir to receive further instructions on the Ale Association Challenge.\n",
[11671]="70021A07\n1\tTalk to Gerthar in Jasmine's Garden\tGerthar is in Jasmine's Garden in Bree. You should speak with Gerthar to continue the the Ale Association Challenge.\n2\tDrink beers (0/6)\tThe beers are in Jasmine's Garden in Bree. Gerthar has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n3\tDrink beers (1/6)\tThe beers are in Jasmine's Garden in Bree. Gerthar has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n4\tDrink beers (2/6)\tThe beers are in Jasmine's Garden in Bree. Gerthar has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n5\tDrink beers (3/6)\tThe beers are in Jasmine's Garden in Bree. Gerthar has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n6\tDrink beers (4/6)\tThe beers are in Jasmine's Garden in Bree. Gerthar has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n7\tDrink beers (5/6)\tThe beers are in Jasmine's Garden in Bree. Gerthar has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n8\tTalk to Gerthar at Jasmine's Garden\tGerthar is in Jasmine's Garden in Bree. You should speak with Gerthar to receive further instructions on the Ale Association Challenge.\n",
[11672]="70021A01\n1\tTalk to Bjarni to begin\tBjarni is in The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree. You should speak with Bjarni to begin the Ale Association Challenge.\n2\tDrink beers (0/6)\tThe beers are in The Prancing Pony in Bree. Bjarni has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n3\tDrink beers (1/6)\tThe beers are in The Prancing Pony in Bree. Bjarni has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n4\tDrink beers (2/6)\tThe beers are in The Prancing Pony in Bree. Bjarni has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n5\tDrink beers (3/6)\tThe beers are in the Prancing Pony in Bree. Bjarni has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n6\tDrink beers (4/6)\tThe beers are in The Prancing Pony in Bree. Bjarni has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n7\tDrink beers (5/6)\tThe beers are in the Prancing Pony in Bree. Bjarni has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n8\tTalk to Bjarni at the Prancing Pony Inn\tBjarni is in The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree. You should speak with Bjarni to receive further instructions on the Ale Association Challenge.\n",
[11673]="70021A08\n1\tTalk to Haddur in the Stone Quarter\tHaddur's tasting area is in the Stone Quarter in Bree. You should speak with Haddur to complete the Ale Association Challenge.\n2\tDrink beers (0/6)\tThe beers are in the Stone Quarter in Bree. Haddur has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n3\tDrink beers (1/6)\tThe beers are in the Stone Quarter in Bree. Haddur has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n4\tDrink beers (2/6)\tThe beers are in the Stone Quarter in Bree. Haddur has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n5\tDrink beers (3/6)\tThe beers are in the Stone Quarter in Bree. Haddur has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n6\tDrink beers (4/6)\tThe beers are in the Stone Quarter in Bree. Haddur has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n7\tDrink beers (5/6)\tThe beers are in the Stone Quarter in Bree. Haddur has challenged you to drink six beers before the time runs out.\n8\tTalk to Haddur in the Stone Quarter\tHaddur is in the Stone Quarter in Bree. You should speak with Haddur to receive further instructions on the Ale Association Challenge.\n",
[11674]="7006C4E7\n1\tComplete Instance: Who Is Our Ally?\tSigênik wishes to ascertain if you paid attention and learned the identity of the elder who is allied with the Rebels in Khûd Zagin. He does not wish to speak within the outpost and suggests you discuss elsewhere.\n2\tSpeak with Sigênik near the north entrance of Jírush\tYou satisfied Sigênik's concerns and correctly identified the elder allied to the rebellion. After returning to Jírush you should speak with Sigênik to learn what is next.\n",
[11675]="7004AB9F\n1\tComplete Bhol Rûdh: Ancient Lights\tCandúr can be found in Udûn. You should talk Candúr.\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted Bhol Rûdh: Ancient Lights.\n",
[11676]="70062263\n1\tSearch the chest\tCedrach has suggested that you search the chest for the Amon family grimoire. The chest is in Cedrach's house, in the Old Forest.\n2\tContinue searching the chest\tWhile searching the chest for the Amon family grimoire you found a blue cloak! Keep searching the chest for the book. The chest is in Cedrach's house, in the Old Forest.\n3\tTell Cedrach you found the book\tYou should let Cedrach know that you found the grimoire at the bottom of the old trunk. Cedrach is in the Old Forest.\n4\tBring the grimoire to Henbran\tCedrach Amon has given you her blessing to take the grimoire to her sister, Henbran, with her apologies for accidentally taking it with her when she left home. Henbran's cottage is in the Old Forest.\n",
[11677]="7004962E\n1\tCollect ancient ward fragments (total: 12)\tAncient ward fragments can be found around Nargroth. You should collect some fragments.\n2\tBring the ward fragments to Isnír\tIsnír can be found at the Udûn Foothold. You should bring the ward fragments to Isnír.\n",
[11678]="70061016\n1\tJourney to the camp-site at Gaerond, in the Angle of Mitheithel\tThe small camp-site at Gaerond is located south of the Trollshaws, in the northern reaches of the Angle.\n2\tTalk to Elladan at Gaerond\tElladan has come to Gaerond, in the Angle.\n",
[11679]="7004E0DA\n1\tComplete 'A Yearly Yield (Intro)'\tEvery day there is something to do during the Anniversary Festival. Come and join everyone and participate in many Anniversary Festival activities for three days!\n2\tComplete 'A Yearly Yield (Intermediate)'\tEvery day there is something to do during the Anniversary Festival. Come and join everyone and participate in many Anniversary Festival activities for three days!\n3\tComplete 'A Yearly Yield (Final)'\tEvery day there is something to do during the Anniversary Festival. Come and join everyone and participate in many Anniversary Festival activities for three days!\n4\tTalk to Waldo Rumble\tWaldo Rumble can be found near the Party Tree in the Shire. You should talk to Waldo Rumble.\n",
[11680]="700350DD\n1\tComplete to receive a map to Bree-town!\tEvery year in the spring, the Anniversary Event takes place to celebrate a very special occasion. Come and join the festivities in Bree-town to help mark this milestone with fireworks and good-cheer!\n2\tComplete to receive a map to Bree-town.\tEvery year in the spring, the Anniversary Event takes place to celebrate a very special occasion. Come and join the festivities in Bree-town and the Shire to help mark this milestone with fireworks and good-cheer!\n",
})
